-- title:
--   Reducedness modulo 1-ζ_q at a supersingular point (H₁ level)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and natural numbers $\ell_g, M'$ with $\ell_g$ prime, $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $M' \neq 0$, $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite. Assume the three variable-change transport hypotheses for the $H_1$ level data over $A_0$: that a $\Gamma_1$-point (an affine point $(x_P,y_P)$ of $W$ with $(\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g})(x_P)=0$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) is carried by $C$ to the transformed datum, that the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$ generator-kernel condition `IsGamma0PowAt` is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`, and that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is preserved in the same way; let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of curves with unit discriminant which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity section, and $\mathcal{T}$ a level transport for Drinfeld pairs at level $q$ satisfying the section-transport identities; assume further that every variable change and every coefficient change of a projective Weierstrass model is realised by a graded ring homomorphism of `projModelGradingCR` satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, resp. `IsCoefficientHom`, and dominating the irrelevant ideal. Let $P_0$ be an absolute fine-moduli package for the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q …`, with ring $B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, and let $x$ be a raw datum over $B_0$ (a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with its $\Gamma_0(M')$ kernel polynomials, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, Drinfeld pair and link condition) whose class in the quotient is the universal point `P₀.univ`. Let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of $B_0$ containing the image of $q$, and let $F_0$ be a formal group over $B_0/\mathfrak{m}$ whose power series is the normalised formal group law of $x$'s curve reduced modulo $\mathfrak{m}$, and suppose the multiplication-by-$q$ series of $F_0$ (the $q$-fold iterate `nthSeries q`) is a unit times $X^{q\cdot q}$. Finally let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $B_0$. Then the quotient of `AdicCompletion 𝔪 P₀.B₀` by the ideal generated by $1-\zeta$ is reduced.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a supersingular point of the $H_1 = \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ moduli problem with full Drinfeld $\Gamma(q)$-structure, that the completed local ring becomes reduced after dividing by $1-\zeta_q$, the Drinfeld local model computation of Katz–Mazur being the source of the hypothesis that the multiplication-by-$q$ series has height two. It feeds the companion statement describing the residue field tensored with this quotient, which is used in the analysis of the reduction of the modular curve in characteristic $q$.
